  "reasoning": "Content Policy Analyst.\nReview audio (transcript) from \"Friends\" app (User pays, Expert is paid host).\nFind violations in three categories: `PlatformMove`, `SuspiciousActivity`, `Explicit-Flirting`.\n\n        *   `PlatformMove`: Proposing/asking to move outside the app, giving/asking for contact info (phone, social media, UPI), proposing to meet.\n        *   `SuspiciousActivity`: Money/payment linked to sexual content/services.\n        *   `Explicit-Flirting`: Sexual talk, requests for nudity, sexual acts, \"open talk\", \"dirty talk\".\n        *   `About a Violation`: Warnings, stories, refusals, negations, questions about rules. (Violation: \"no\", Confidence $\\le 0.3$).\n\n        *   Ordinary conversation (greetings, small talk, work, family, location).\n        *   Internal app call types (video call, \"call me\").\n        *   \"Normal talk\" (non-sexual).\n        *   Apps mentioned for other reasons.\n        *   Meeting other people (not the other person).\n        *   Personal details without contact info.\n        *   Compliments (\"sexy voice\", \"beautiful\").\n        *   Relationship talk (\"I love you\", \"girlfriend\").\n        *   \"Show/open\" for non-body things.\n        *   Refusals of sexual talk.\nJSON object, minified, specific fields (`t`, `seg`, `tr`, `f`, `spk`, `ctx`, `speech_act`, `j`, `violation`, `c`).\n\n    *   [00:00 - 01:30]: Greetings, location (Mysore, Bangalore), work (Bank - Bandhan, Jana Small Finance), area (K.R. Puram, Koramangala), shift/leave status. -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [01:31 - 02:30]: Hometown (Davangere), marital status (one is married, one is in PG), job role (Area Manager), salary (80-85k). -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [02:31 - 03:20]: Days off, using the app (boredom), adjusting to Bangalore. -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [03:21 - 04:10]: Weekend activities (making dosa), PG food, location details (Kolar, Kuppam). -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [04:11 - 05:40]: Work history (iPhone factory, Tata Electronics, Gold loans, sales/operations). -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [05:41 - 06:10]: Gold loan discussion, location (Koramangala), incentives. -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [06:11 - 07:00]: Family, baby (boy), travel to hometown (car vs train). -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [07:01 - 08:20]: Travel plans, festivals (Panchami), weekends, being unwell. -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [08:21 - 10:40]: Detailed discussion about gold loan operations, customer follow-ups, branch management, interest payments, auctions. -> *Ordinary conversation (work-related). Allowed.*\n    *   [10:41 - 11:15]: Department discussion (NPA, OD, Collection). -> *Ordinary conversation. Allowed.*\n    *   [11:16 - 11:43]: Discussion about supervisors and branch managers.\n        *   [11:38] \"They call me and give me a number, I will give it to you.\"\n            *   *Analysis:* The speaker is talking about their work experience. \"They [supervisors/managers] call me and give me a number [of a customer], I will give it to you [the customer/the process].\"\n            *   *Context:* The conversation is about the NPA/Collection department. The speaker is describing how they get lead numbers for collection.\n            *   *Is it a PlatformMove?* No. They are not proposing to move the conversation with the *current* caller to another app or giving the *caller's* number. They are describing a work process involving customer numbers.\n            *   *Is it a violation?* No. It's a story/description of work.\n\n    *   Did I miss any \"WhatsApp\", \"Telegram\", \"Instagram\"? No.\n    *   Did I miss any phone numbers? No.\n    *   Did I miss any \"meet in person\"? No.\n    *   Did I miss any \"rate\", \"pay\", \"money\" for sex? No.\n    *   Did I miss any \"open talk\", \"dirty talk\", \"show me\"? No.\n    *   The conversation is almost entirely professional/small talk about banking jobs in Bangalore.\n\n    *   The transcript contains no violations of `PlatformMove`, `SuspiciousActivity`, or `Explicit-Flirting`.\n    *   The mention of \"give me a number\" at the end is clearly in the context of bank collection work, not moving the app contact.\n\n    *   Return `{\"d\": []}`.",
